1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,008
Today's video is all about my journey across Japan... by handcart!

2
00:00:10,008 --> 00:00:11,508
Scene 1: Journey Across Japan – From North to South

3
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:12,908
Hello!

4
00:00:12,930 --> 00:00:16,297
I’m John.

5
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:19,287
I’m visiting from abroad.

6
00:00:19,310 --> 00:00:22,950
Starting today, I’ll be traveling across Japan.

7
00:00:22,973 --> 00:00:26,950
I love Japan’s nature.

8
00:00:26,973 --> 00:00:30,340
And I adore the people here too.

9
00:00:30,363 --> 00:00:35,196
I’ll be pulling this handcart all the way from north to south.

10
00:00:35,219 --> 00:00:38,306
Walking the entire length of Japan.

11
00:00:38,330 --> 00:00:41,296
It’s going to be a long journey.

12
00:00:41,319 --> 00:00:45,853
I’m a little nervous, but I’m really excited!

13
00:00:45,876 --> 00:00:51,409
I’ll be filming every day and sharing it online.

14
00:00:51,432 --> 00:00:56,265
Right now, I’m at Cape Sōya in Hokkaido.

15
00:00:56,288 --> 00:00:59,655
The ocean here is stunning.

16
00:00:59,678 --> 00:01:02,945
The wind’s a bit chilly, though.

17
00:01:02,967 --> 00:01:06,301
But the sky’s clear—perfect weather!

18
00:01:06,324 --> 00:01:09,333
Oh! There’s someone over there.

19
00:01:09,356 --> 00:01:12,290
Let’s go talk to them.

20
00:01:12,313 --> 00:01:14,587
Hello!

21
00:01:14,610 --> 00:01:16,186
Hello!

22
00:01:16,209 --> 00:01:18,818
That’s a big load you’ve got there!

23
00:01:18,841 --> 00:01:23,241
Yeah! This is my handcart.

24
00:01:23,264 --> 00:01:26,081
What’s inside?

25
00:01:26,105 --> 00:01:29,143
A tent and some clothes.

26
00:01:29,166 --> 00:01:31,299
I see.

27
00:01:31,322 --> 00:01:33,356
Is it heavy?

28
00:01:33,379 --> 00:01:37,179
Oh yeah, super heavy.

29
00:01:37,202 --> 00:01:40,054
When did you arrive in Japan?

30
00:01:40,077 --> 00:01:43,211
Last Friday.

31
00:01:43,234 --> 00:01:45,327
I see.

32
00:01:45,351 --> 00:01:47,751
Did you come alone?

33
00:01:47,774 --> 00:01:51,507
Yep, just me.

34
00:01:51,530 --> 00:01:54,463
This is Cape Sōya.

35
00:01:54,486 --> 00:01:57,420
It’s the northernmost point of Japan.

36
00:01:57,443 --> 00:02:00,048
I know!

37
00:02:00,071 --> 00:02:02,804
It’s such a beautiful place.

38
00:02:02,827 --> 00:02:05,294
Thanks!

39
00:02:05,317 --> 00:02:08,318
Where are you heading next?

40
00:02:08,342 --> 00:02:11,375
All the way down south.

41
00:02:11,398 --> 00:02:13,765
Are you walking the whole way?

42
00:02:13,788 --> 00:02:17,462
Yep, walking the whole way.

43
00:02:17,485 --> 00:02:19,897
That sounds tough.

44
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:23,254
It is a little.

45
00:02:23,278 --> 00:02:25,612
But it’s fun!

46
00:02:25,635 --> 00:02:29,068
Do you like Japanese food?

47
00:02:29,091 --> 00:02:32,358
Oh yeah, I love it.

48
00:02:32,381 --> 00:02:35,056
What’s your favorite?

49
00:02:35,079 --> 00:02:37,948
Sushi, hands down.

50
00:02:37,971 --> 00:02:40,009
I see.

51
00:02:40,033 --> 00:02:43,837
Hokkaido’s seafood is amazing, by the way.

52
00:02:43,860 --> 00:02:46,094
Really?

53
00:02:46,117 --> 00:02:49,150
I’d love to try a local restaurant later.

54
00:02:49,173 --> 00:02:51,310
You absolutely should!

55
00:02:51,334 --> 00:02:54,801
Are you taking pictures with that camera?

56
00:02:54,824 --> 00:02:58,824
Yes, I’m a blogger.

57
00:02:58,847 --> 00:03:01,413
I film videos every day.

58
00:03:01,436 --> 00:03:04,170
That’s interesting!

59
00:03:04,193 --> 00:03:08,593
I introduce various places in Japan online.

60
00:03:08,615 --> 00:03:11,215
That’s amazing!

61
00:03:11,238 --> 00:03:15,272
Please introduce my town too!

62
00:03:15,295 --> 00:03:18,431
Yes, of course I will.

63
00:03:18,454 --> 00:03:21,687
When are you leaving?

64
00:03:21,710 --> 00:03:24,143
I’m leaving right now.

65
00:03:24,166 --> 00:03:25,933
I see.

66
00:03:25,956 --> 00:03:28,023
Good luck!

67
00:03:28,046 --> 00:03:30,212
Thanks!

68
00:03:30,235 --> 00:03:35,002
It’s cold out, so be careful not to catch a cold.

69
00:03:35,025 --> 00:03:37,825
Yes, I’ll be careful.

70
00:03:37,848 --> 00:03:40,381
Watch out for cars.

71
00:03:40,404 --> 00:03:43,404
Okay, I’ll walk slowly.

72
00:03:43,427 --> 00:03:45,661
Have a great trip!

73
00:03:45,684 --> 00:03:47,817
Thanks!

74
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:56,849
You can download today’s script from the description and top comments. Please leave a comment before downloading!

75
00:03:56,849 --> 00:03:58,349
Scene 2: A Day in Furano

76
00:03:58,349 --> 00:03:59,786
Hello!

77
00:03:59,810 --> 00:04:03,343
I’m John.

78
00:04:03,366 --> 00:04:06,899
I’m pulling my cart and walking again today.

79
00:04:06,922 --> 00:04:11,056
This is Furano, Hokkaido.

80
00:04:11,079 --> 00:04:14,212
The mountains are so beautiful.

81
00:04:14,235 --> 00:04:18,130
But the roads are a bit tough.

82
00:04:18,153 --> 00:04:22,153
Because my cart is really heavy.

83
00:04:22,176 --> 00:04:24,943
I’ve walked a lot today.

84
00:04:24,966 --> 00:04:27,566
I’m really tired.

85
00:04:27,589 --> 00:04:30,355
Let’s take a short break.

86
00:04:30,378 --> 00:04:34,465
Oh, there’s someone over there.

87
00:04:34,489 --> 00:04:36,546
It’s an elderly woman.

88
00:04:36,570 --> 00:04:39,170
Let’s go talk to them.

89
00:04:39,193 --> 00:04:41,003
Hello!

90
00:04:41,026 --> 00:04:42,826
Hello!

91
00:04:42,849 --> 00:04:45,716
That’s a big load you’ve got there!

92
00:04:45,739 --> 00:04:49,153
Yeah! This is my handcart.

93
00:04:49,176 --> 00:04:51,983
What’s inside?

94
00:04:52,006 --> 00:04:54,940
She has a tent, clothes, and a camera.

95
00:04:54,963 --> 00:04:57,296
That must be really heavy.

96
00:04:57,319 --> 00:05:00,387
Oh yeah, super heavy.

97
00:05:00,410 --> 00:05:02,659
Where did you come from?

98
00:05:02,683 --> 00:05:05,172
I came from Cape Sōya.

99
00:05:05,196 --> 00:05:07,439
Did you walk all the way?

100
00:05:07,463 --> 00:05:10,996
Yes, I walked the whole way.

101
00:05:11,019 --> 00:05:13,419
That sounds tough.

102
00:05:13,442 --> 00:05:16,447
Yes. A little tired, though.

103
00:05:16,470 --> 00:05:19,948
I live nearby.

104
00:05:19,971 --> 00:05:23,063
This place is really beautiful.

105
00:05:23,086 --> 00:05:27,320
Yeah. Please rest here for a bit.

106
00:05:27,343 --> 00:05:29,280
Thanks!

107
00:05:29,304 --> 00:05:32,037
Just a moment, please.

108
00:05:32,060 --> 00:05:33,227
Okay.

109
00:05:33,250 --> 00:05:36,067
Here, please take this.

110
00:05:36,091 --> 00:05:38,528
Is this a melon?

111
00:05:38,551 --> 00:05:41,818
Yes. It’s Furano melon.

112
00:05:41,841 --> 00:05:45,475
Wow, it’s huge!

113
00:05:45,499 --> 00:05:49,573
Yeah. It’s sweet and delicious.

114
00:05:49,596 --> 00:05:51,207
Thanks!

115
00:05:51,231 --> 00:05:54,031
Please have some of these tomatoes too.

116
00:05:54,054 --> 00:05:55,587
Tomatoes too?

117
00:05:55,610 --> 00:05:58,943
Yeah. I grew them myself.

118
00:05:58,966 --> 00:06:01,933
Wow, I’m so happy!

119
00:06:01,956 --> 00:06:04,689
Here, please eat.

120
00:06:04,712 --> 00:06:07,361
Yes, I’ll have some.

121
00:06:07,384 --> 00:06:09,918
It’s really delicious.

122
00:06:09,941 --> 00:06:11,907
I’m glad.

123
00:06:11,930 --> 00:06:15,297
I got some delicious melon and tomatoes.

124
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:18,153
Thank you so much.

125
00:06:18,176 --> 00:06:22,376
No problem. Where are you heading next?

126
00:06:22,399 --> 00:06:24,733
I’m heading south.

127
00:06:24,756 --> 00:06:27,029
That’s quite a journey.

128
00:06:27,052 --> 00:06:32,052
Yeah, but I love the Japanese people, so it’s fun.

129
00:06:32,075 --> 00:06:35,008
Please be careful around cars.

130
00:06:35,031 --> 00:06:37,598
Yes, I’ll be careful.

131
00:06:37,621 --> 00:06:39,297
Good luck!

132
00:06:39,321 --> 00:06:42,607
I got some energy from Grandma.

133
00:06:42,630 --> 00:06:44,963
Thank you so much.

134
00:06:44,986 --> 00:06:46,953
Have a great trip!

135
00:06:46,976 --> 00:06:49,552
Okay, I’m off now.

136
00:06:49,575 --> 00:06:56,680
Check the link in the description and top comments to review today’s video! ※The site may be removed without notice.

137
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:58,180
Scene 3: A Stroll Through Hakodate's Morning Market

138
00:06:58,180 --> 00:06:59,980
Hello!

139
00:07:00,003 --> 00:07:04,003
I’m John.

140
00:07:04,026 --> 00:07:08,226
I’m pulling my cart and walking again today.

141
00:07:08,249 --> 00:07:12,449
This is Hakodate, Hokkaido.

142
00:07:12,472 --> 00:07:17,344
It’s close to the sea, so the scenery is beautiful.

143
00:07:17,368 --> 00:07:21,987
But the roads are a bit tough.

144
00:07:22,010 --> 00:07:24,650
I’ve walked a lot today.

145
00:07:24,673 --> 00:07:27,873
You look a bit tired.

146
00:07:27,896 --> 00:07:32,296
Oh, is there a festival here?

147
00:07:32,319 --> 00:07:35,497
There are so many people!

148
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:39,054
It says ‘morning market.’

149
00:07:39,077 --> 00:07:42,610
There are all kinds of shops here.

150
00:07:42,633 --> 00:07:46,633
There’s lots of fish and crab!

151
00:07:46,656 --> 00:07:49,389
It looks so delicious.

152
00:07:49,412 --> 00:07:52,667
Let’s take a look around.

153
00:07:52,691 --> 00:08:00,534
Oh, there’s a lively shop owner with lots of customers over there!

154
00:08:00,557 --> 00:08:02,691
Let’s go talk to them.

155
00:08:02,714 --> 00:08:04,385
Hello!

156
00:08:04,408 --> 00:08:06,447
Welcome!

157
00:08:06,470 --> 00:08:08,704
Fresh fish here!

158
00:08:08,727 --> 00:08:10,693
We’ve got crab too!

159
00:08:10,716 --> 00:08:14,050
Wow, that’s amazing!

160
00:08:14,073 --> 00:08:17,439
There’s so much crab!

161
00:08:17,462 --> 00:08:20,910
Hey, where did you come from?

162
00:08:20,934 --> 00:08:23,500
That’s a big load you’ve got there.

163
00:08:23,523 --> 00:08:27,462
I came from abroad.

164
00:08:27,485 --> 00:08:32,020
I’m traveling around Japan pulling a cart.

165
00:08:32,044 --> 00:08:34,844
Wow, that’s impressive.

166
00:08:34,867 --> 00:08:36,884
With a cart?

167
00:08:36,907 --> 00:08:39,074
That must be tough.

168
00:08:39,097 --> 00:08:42,830
It is a little.

169
00:08:42,853 --> 00:08:45,733
But it’s fun!

170
00:08:45,756 --> 00:08:49,889
I see, I see. You’re working hard!

171
00:08:49,912 --> 00:08:53,879
This is Hakodate’s morning market.

172
00:08:53,902 --> 00:08:57,993
There’s plenty of delicious seafood here.

173
00:08:58,016 --> 00:09:02,550
Yeah, I’m hungry.

174
00:09:02,573 --> 00:09:05,547
I’d like to eat something.

175
00:09:05,570 --> 00:09:08,903
How about a seafood rice bowl?

176
00:09:08,926 --> 00:09:14,198
It’s loaded with fresh fish and salmon roe!

177
00:09:14,221 --> 00:09:16,705
A seafood rice bowl?

178
00:09:16,729 --> 00:09:18,821
That sounds great.

179
00:09:18,845 --> 00:09:20,645
It looks delicious.

180
00:09:20,668 --> 00:09:25,468
Yeah, our seafood rice bowl is the best!

181
00:09:25,491 --> 00:09:27,024
Want some?

182
00:09:27,047 --> 00:09:31,380
Yes, but isn’t it a bit expensive?

183
00:09:31,403 --> 00:09:34,216
It’s fine.

184
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:39,240
You’ve been working hard, so I’ll give you a special discount.

185
00:09:39,263 --> 00:09:40,833
Really?

186
00:09:40,857 --> 00:09:42,590
Thanks!

187
00:09:42,613 --> 00:09:44,546
How much is it?

188
00:09:44,569 --> 00:09:49,403
Normally it’s 2,500 yen, but how about 2,000 yen?

189
00:09:49,426 --> 00:09:53,396
Can’t it be a little cheaper?

190
00:09:53,419 --> 00:09:56,953
How about 1,500 yen?

191
00:09:56,976 --> 00:10:00,427
1,500 yen, huh...

192
00:10:00,450 --> 00:10:03,927
Okay, it’s a deal.

193
00:10:03,951 --> 00:10:06,717
Wow, thank you so much!

194
00:10:06,740 --> 00:10:09,830
Here you go, please eat.

195
00:10:09,854 --> 00:10:12,891
Yes, I’ll have some.

196
00:10:12,914 --> 00:10:15,958
It’s delicious!

197
00:10:15,982 --> 00:10:18,648
The fish is so fresh.

198
00:10:18,671 --> 00:10:20,838
Right?

199
00:10:20,861 --> 00:10:24,513
Eat up and keep going strong!

200
00:10:24,537 --> 00:10:27,737
Yes, I feel energized!

201
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:29,442
Thanks!

202
00:10:29,465 --> 00:10:32,924
Have a safe trip!

203
00:10:32,947 --> 00:10:35,815
Thank you so much.

204
00:10:35,838 --> 00:10:37,438
I’m off!

205
00:10:37,461 --> 00:10:42,628
I had an amazing seafood bowl at the morning market.

206
00:10:42,651 --> 00:10:46,851
The shopkeeper was really kind too.

207
00:10:46,874 --> 00:10:50,840
I feel refreshed, so I’ll keep walking with renewed energy.

208
00:10:50,863 --> 00:10:52,363
Scene 4: Ferry Journey: From Hokkaido to Honshu

209
00:10:52,363 --> 00:10:53,802
Hello!

210
00:10:53,826 --> 00:10:57,364
I’m John.

211
00:10:57,388 --> 00:11:01,954
Right now, I’m at the ferry terminal in Hakodate.

212
00:11:01,977 --> 00:11:05,818
I’m about to board the ferry.

213
00:11:05,842 --> 00:11:09,978
I’ll even bring this heavy cart with me.

214
00:11:10,002 --> 00:11:14,020
The ferry is huge inside.

215
00:11:14,044 --> 00:11:17,486
There are shops and restaurants too.

216
00:11:17,510 --> 00:11:20,789
You can see the ocean from the window.

217
00:11:20,813 --> 00:11:23,613
It’s so beautiful.

218
00:11:23,635 --> 00:11:30,269
The ferry ride from Hokkaido to Aomori takes about 4 hours.

219
00:11:30,292 --> 00:11:32,825
I’ll take a little nap.

220
00:11:32,848 --> 00:11:36,415
Well, we’ve arrived in Aomori.

221
00:11:36,438 --> 00:11:39,277
Finally, Honshu!

222
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:42,772
I’ll keep pulling my cart and walking.

223
00:11:42,796 --> 00:11:46,878
Look, there are so many apple trees over there.

224
00:11:46,901 --> 00:11:50,587
The red apples look gorgeous.

225
00:11:50,611 --> 00:11:53,044
There’s someone there.

226
00:11:53,067 --> 00:11:55,034
Let’s talk to them.

227
00:11:55,057 --> 00:11:57,092
Hello!

228
00:11:57,115 --> 00:11:58,715
Hello!

229
00:11:58,738 --> 00:12:01,711
That’s a big load you’ve got there!

230
00:12:01,735 --> 00:12:05,614
Yes, this is a cart.

231
00:12:05,637 --> 00:12:07,919
That’s impressive!

232
00:12:07,942 --> 00:12:10,417
Where did you come from?

233
00:12:10,441 --> 00:12:13,208
I came from Hokkaido.

234
00:12:13,231 --> 00:12:16,504
How did you cross the sea?

235
00:12:16,527 --> 00:12:21,094
I took a ferry from Hakodate to Aomori.

236
00:12:21,118 --> 00:12:23,335
A ferry?

237
00:12:23,359 --> 00:12:26,796
How long did it take?

238
00:12:26,819 --> 00:12:29,822
It took about 4 hours.

239
00:12:29,846 --> 00:12:34,213
I took a little nap on the ferry.

240
00:12:34,236 --> 00:12:36,040
I see.

241
00:12:36,063 --> 00:12:39,097
Where are you heading to?

242
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:42,202
All the way down south.

243
00:12:42,225 --> 00:12:44,758
Are you walking there?

244
00:12:44,781 --> 00:12:48,114
Yep, walking the whole way.

245
00:12:48,137 --> 00:12:50,591
That sounds tough.

246
00:12:50,615 --> 00:12:54,215
I grow apples here.

247
00:12:54,238 --> 00:12:56,887
Ah, those are Aomori apples!

248
00:12:56,911 --> 00:12:59,178
They’re very famous.

249
00:12:59,201 --> 00:13:03,536
Yes, I’m about to transport these apples now.

250
00:13:03,560 --> 00:13:06,693
Where are you taking them from and to?

251
00:13:06,716 --> 00:13:12,049
From here to a factory near the train station.

252
00:13:12,072 --> 00:13:14,049
How are you transporting them?

253
00:13:14,072 --> 00:13:17,072
By truck.

254
00:13:17,095 --> 00:13:20,269
Is it far from here to the factory?

255
00:13:20,293 --> 00:13:24,827
No, it’s about 20 minutes by truck.

256
00:13:24,850 --> 00:13:26,816
I see.

257
00:13:26,839 --> 00:13:30,489
You must have a lot of apples—it must be tough.

258
00:13:30,513 --> 00:13:34,113
Yeah, it’s a bit tough.

259
00:13:34,136 --> 00:13:36,503
Are you thirsty?

260
00:13:36,526 --> 00:13:39,822
Yes, a little.

261
00:13:39,845 --> 00:13:44,179
Here, have some of this apple juice.

262
00:13:44,201 --> 00:13:46,068
Really? You made it?

263
00:13:46,091 --> 00:13:47,658
Thanks!

264
00:13:47,681 --> 00:13:50,447
I made it with my own apples.

265
00:13:50,470 --> 00:13:53,237
It’s 100% pure juice.

266
00:13:53,260 --> 00:13:55,427
Thank you!

267
00:13:55,450 --> 00:13:59,332
Wow, it’s so sweet and delicious!

268
00:13:59,355 --> 00:14:01,531
I’m glad.

269
00:14:01,554 --> 00:14:03,788
Do you feel refreshed now?

270
00:14:03,811 --> 00:14:07,011
Yes, I feel energized!

271
00:14:07,034 --> 00:14:10,034
Where are you walking to next?

272
00:14:10,057 --> 00:14:13,715
Today, I’m walking to that town over there.

273
00:14:13,738 --> 00:14:17,138
Be careful out there!

274
00:14:17,161 --> 00:14:20,495
Yes, I’ll watch out for cars.

275
00:14:20,518 --> 00:14:22,651
Have a great trip!

276
00:14:22,674 --> 00:14:24,274
Thank you!

277
00:14:24,297 --> 00:14:26,144
I’m off!

278
00:14:26,167 --> 00:14:29,665
I got such delicious apple juice!

279
00:14:29,689 --> 00:14:32,938
The ferry ride was fun too.

280
00:14:32,961 --> 00:14:36,695
I’m really looking forward to exploring Honshu as well.

281
00:14:36,718 --> 00:14:39,518
I’ll keep walking energetically today.

282
00:14:39,541 --> 00:14:41,041
Scene 5: A Rainy Day Shelter

283
00:14:41,041 --> 00:14:42,841
Hello!

284
00:14:42,864 --> 00:14:46,397
I’m John.

285
00:14:46,420 --> 00:14:50,820
I’m pulling my cart and walking again today.

286
00:14:50,844 --> 00:14:54,010
This is Akita.

287
00:14:54,033 --> 00:14:56,800
It was cloudy since morning.

288
00:14:56,823 --> 00:15:01,673
And it started raining a little while ago.

289
00:15:01,696 --> 00:15:05,032
The wind is a bit strong too.

290
00:15:05,055 --> 00:15:09,466
My clothes are soaked, and it’s freezing.

291
00:15:09,490 --> 00:15:12,862
Pulling the cart is tough.

292
00:15:12,885 --> 00:15:17,851
Oh, there’s a café over there!

293
00:15:17,874 --> 00:15:20,125
It says ‘Café’ on the sign.

294
00:15:20,148 --> 00:15:23,391
Let’s take shelter from the rain there.

295
00:15:23,415 --> 00:15:26,948
I’d love to have some warm coffee too.

296
00:15:26,971 --> 00:15:29,638
Let’s go inside.

297
00:15:29,661 --> 00:15:31,461
Hello!

298
00:15:31,484 --> 00:15:33,663
Welcome!

299
00:15:33,686 --> 00:15:36,521
Please come in.

300
00:15:36,545 --> 00:15:38,151
Thanks!

301
00:15:38,175 --> 00:15:41,808
It’s raining hard outside, huh?

302
00:15:41,831 --> 00:15:43,798
Yeah, it suddenly started pouring.

303
00:15:43,820 --> 00:15:47,293
It came down really hard all of a sudden.

304
00:15:47,317 --> 00:15:51,403
Yeah, it's pouring out there.

305
00:15:51,426 --> 00:15:53,793
Your clothes are soaked.

306
00:15:53,817 --> 00:15:55,393
Are you okay?

307
00:15:55,416 --> 00:15:58,583
Yeah, I'm fine.

308
00:15:58,606 --> 00:16:01,773
But it's a bit chilly.

309
00:16:01,796 --> 00:16:05,930
It's windy today too, so it feels cold.

310
00:16:05,953 --> 00:16:09,887
Yeah, it really is freezing.

311
00:16:09,910 --> 00:16:12,876
Please, take a seat over here.

312
00:16:12,899 --> 00:16:15,433
I'll grab a towel for you.

313
00:16:15,456 --> 00:16:17,473
Thanks!

314
00:16:17,496 --> 00:16:20,096
Here you go.

315
00:16:20,119 --> 00:16:21,977
Use this one.

316
00:16:22,001 --> 00:16:24,656
That's so kind of you.

317
00:16:24,679 --> 00:16:26,691
I really appreciate it.

318
00:16:26,715 --> 00:16:29,649
What would you like to order?

319
00:16:29,672 --> 00:16:33,166
I'll have a hot coffee, please.

320
00:16:33,189 --> 00:16:36,464
Got it. Hot coffee, coming right up.

321
00:16:36,487 --> 00:16:39,254
Please wait just a moment.

322
00:16:39,277 --> 00:16:42,451
Is your cart outside okay?

323
00:16:42,474 --> 00:16:46,841
Yeah, you can leave it right in front of the shop.

324
00:16:46,864 --> 00:16:49,551
That’s a big load you’ve got there!

325
00:16:49,575 --> 00:16:53,212
It's my travel luggage.

326
00:16:53,235 --> 00:16:55,968
Are you traveling?

327
00:16:55,991 --> 00:16:57,650
That’s impressive!

328
00:16:57,673 --> 00:17:02,607
Yeah, I'm walking from one end of Japan to the other.

329
00:17:02,630 --> 00:17:04,521
Walking? Wow.

330
00:17:04,544 --> 00:17:07,160
That sounds tough.

331
00:17:07,184 --> 00:17:10,634
It is a little.

332
00:17:10,658 --> 00:17:15,466
But it's fun seeing all the different towns along the way.

333
00:17:15,489 --> 00:17:17,569
Here you go.

334
00:17:17,593 --> 00:17:20,070
Your hot coffee.

335
00:17:20,094 --> 00:17:23,428
Wow, it smells amazing!

336
00:17:23,451 --> 00:17:27,418
Please, drink it while it's still warm.

337
00:17:27,441 --> 00:17:29,441
Thank you!

338
00:17:29,464 --> 00:17:32,242
This coffee is delicious.

339
00:17:32,266 --> 00:17:34,840
I’m glad.

340
00:17:34,863 --> 00:17:37,697
Feeling a little warmer now?

341
00:17:37,721 --> 00:17:40,808
Yeah, I am.

342
00:17:40,831 --> 00:17:43,031
I feel much better.

343
00:17:43,054 --> 00:17:46,487
It's still raining hard outside.

344
00:17:46,510 --> 00:17:48,360
Yeah, it suddenly started pouring.

345
00:17:48,384 --> 00:17:51,317
Looks like it's not letting up anytime soon.

346
00:17:51,340 --> 00:17:55,940
Take your time and relax until the rain stops.

347
00:17:55,963 --> 00:17:57,763
Thanks!

348
00:17:57,786 --> 00:17:59,591
I will.

349
00:17:59,615 --> 00:18:04,582
Oh, the sky's starting to brighten a bit.

350
00:18:04,605 --> 00:18:06,538
You're right.

351
00:18:06,561 --> 00:18:09,394
The rain's letting up.

352
00:18:09,417 --> 00:18:14,018
Yeah, it should stop soon.

353
00:18:14,041 --> 00:18:15,841
I’m glad.

354
00:18:15,864 --> 00:18:18,731
I should get ready to head out soon.

355
00:18:18,754 --> 00:18:21,587
Where are you heading next?

356
00:18:21,610 --> 00:18:25,281
I'll keep walking south.

357
00:18:25,305 --> 00:18:30,471
The roads are wet, so watch your step.

358
00:18:30,494 --> 00:18:33,228
Yes, I’ll be careful.

359
00:18:33,251 --> 00:18:37,051
Have a great trip. I'm rooting for you!

360
00:18:37,074 --> 00:18:39,640
Thank you so much.

361
00:18:39,663 --> 00:18:41,433
I’m off!

362
00:18:41,457 --> 00:18:45,351
The café staff were so kind.

363
00:18:45,374 --> 00:18:50,019
Drinking that warm coffee really cheered me up.

364
00:18:50,043 --> 00:18:54,076
Outside, the rain has stopped, and blue skies are peeking through.

365
00:18:54,099 --> 00:18:58,705
I'll keep walking toward the next town—time to keep going!

366
00:18:58,728 --> 00:19:00,228
Scene 6: Taking on the Challenge of Wanko Soba

367
00:19:00,228 --> 00:19:05,967
Hi there! I'm John.

368
00:19:05,991 --> 00:19:09,686
I’m pulling my cart and walking again today.

369
00:19:09,710 --> 00:19:12,843
I'm in Iwate right now.

370
00:19:12,866 --> 00:19:15,514
I'm starving.

371
00:19:15,538 --> 00:19:19,419
Today, I'm having something special.

372
00:19:19,442 --> 00:19:22,842
It's called *wanko soba*—a bowl of noodles you eat in one go!

373
00:19:22,865 --> 00:19:26,032
I want to eat as many as I can.

374
00:19:26,055 --> 00:19:29,388
Let's head inside the shop.

375
00:19:29,411 --> 00:19:32,895
Hello! Hello!

376
00:19:32,919 --> 00:19:35,319
You're trying *wanko soba*, huh?

377
00:19:35,342 --> 00:19:38,175
Yeah, that's right!

378
00:19:38,198 --> 00:19:40,637
I'm eating it too—let's tackle this together!

379
00:19:40,661 --> 00:19:42,935
Sounds good to me!

380
00:19:42,958 --> 00:19:44,850
Thanks!

381
00:19:44,874 --> 00:19:47,561
Nice to meet you!

382
00:19:47,584 --> 00:19:50,117
That’s a big load you’ve got there!

383
00:19:50,140 --> 00:19:51,974
Are you traveling?

384
00:19:51,997 --> 00:19:57,654
Yep! I'm pulling a cart and walking across Japan.

385
00:19:57,677 --> 00:19:59,755
That’s impressive!

386
00:19:59,779 --> 00:20:02,180
Where did you come from?

387
00:20:02,203 --> 00:20:05,270
I’m visiting from abroad.

388
00:20:05,293 --> 00:20:08,260
From north to south.

389
00:20:08,283 --> 00:20:11,283
Is traveling in Japan fun?

390
00:20:11,306 --> 00:20:15,001
Yeah, it's a blast!

391
00:20:15,024 --> 00:20:17,157
What are your hobbies?

392
00:20:17,180 --> 00:20:21,014
I love traveling.

393
00:20:21,037 --> 00:20:24,690
And I also enjoy taking photos.

394
00:20:24,714 --> 00:20:26,550
Photos?

395
00:20:26,573 --> 00:20:28,221
That sounds great.

396
00:20:28,244 --> 00:20:32,411
Yep! I share them online.

397
00:20:32,434 --> 00:20:35,800
What about you? What do you like to do?

398
00:20:35,823 --> 00:20:39,290
I love eating.

399
00:20:39,313 --> 00:20:41,080
You love eating?

400
00:20:41,103 --> 00:20:44,536
There’s so much delicious food out there!

401
00:20:44,559 --> 00:20:47,438
Yeah, I love traveling too.

402
00:20:47,462 --> 00:20:50,195
I go out to eat all the good stuff.

403
00:20:50,219 --> 00:20:52,857
That’s an amazing hobby!

404
00:20:52,880 --> 00:20:56,413
Today, I’m going to eat a ton of *wanko soba*.

405
00:20:56,436 --> 00:20:59,036
How many bowls are you aiming for?

406
00:20:59,059 --> 00:21:01,260
100 bowls!

407
00:21:01,284 --> 00:21:03,217
100 bowls? That’s incredible!

408
00:21:03,240 --> 00:21:05,727
That’s amazing!

409
00:21:05,750 --> 00:21:09,084
How many bowls are you planning to eat?

410
00:21:09,108 --> 00:21:13,150
I’d like to eat about 50.

411
00:21:13,173 --> 00:21:15,342
You can eat more than that!

412
00:21:15,365 --> 00:21:17,099
Good luck!

413
00:21:17,121 --> 00:21:19,888
Yeah, I’ll do my best!

414
00:21:19,911 --> 00:21:22,956
Oh, the noodles are here!

415
00:21:22,980 --> 00:21:25,036
Thank you!

416
00:21:25,060 --> 00:21:26,993
This is delicious!

417
00:21:27,016 --> 00:21:30,149
But they keep coming fast!

418
00:21:30,172 --> 00:21:33,306
Yep, I’m eating nonstop.

419
00:21:33,329 --> 00:21:36,062
That’s tough!

420
00:21:36,085 --> 00:21:37,899
Yeah, it suddenly started pouring.

421
00:21:37,923 --> 00:21:40,190
But it’s fun!

422
00:21:40,213 --> 00:21:44,013
Wow, I’m stuffed!

423
00:21:44,036 --> 00:21:46,169
How many bowls did you eat?

424
00:21:46,192 --> 00:21:48,792
I ate 60!

425
00:21:48,815 --> 00:21:51,348
I can’t eat another bite.

426
00:21:51,371 --> 00:21:53,343
That’s impressive!

427
00:21:53,366 --> 00:21:55,533
You did great!

428
00:21:55,556 --> 00:21:57,827
Thanks!

429
00:21:57,851 --> 00:22:00,496
You’re amazing!

430
00:22:00,520 --> 00:22:04,014
Yeah, I ate 100 bowls.

431
00:22:04,037 --> 00:22:06,689
That’s incredible!

432
00:22:06,713 --> 00:22:09,386
It was a great experience.

433
00:22:09,410 --> 00:22:13,143
Wanko soba was absolutely delicious.

434
00:22:13,166 --> 00:22:16,501
And it was so much fun!

435
00:22:16,525 --> 00:22:20,291
I even made new friends.

436
00:22:20,314 --> 00:22:25,148
My stomach’s full, so I’ll take it easy today.

437
00:22:25,171 --> 00:22:28,704
I’ll keep walking tomorrow too—give it my all!

438
00:22:28,727 --> 00:22:30,227
Scene 7: Scenic Matsushima and Photo Taking

439
00:22:30,227 --> 00:22:31,869
Hello!

440
00:22:31,893 --> 00:22:35,262
I’m John.

441
00:22:35,285 --> 00:22:39,152
We’re in Matsushima, Miyagi today.

442
00:22:39,175 --> 00:22:42,177
The ocean is so beautiful.

443
00:22:42,200 --> 00:22:45,138
There are so many tiny islands.

444
00:22:45,162 --> 00:22:47,836
The view is stunning!

445
00:22:47,860 --> 00:22:50,869
The breeze feels amazing too.

446
00:22:50,893 --> 00:22:53,980
This is a super famous spot.

447
00:22:54,004 --> 00:22:56,937
I took tons of photos.

448
00:22:56,960 --> 00:23:01,127
Oh, I’d love to take a photo with you too!

449
00:23:01,150 --> 00:23:03,683
There’s someone over there.

450
00:23:03,706 --> 00:23:05,839
Let’s ask them!

451
00:23:05,862 --> 00:23:08,262
Excuse me!

452
00:23:08,285 --> 00:23:10,885
Yes, what can I do for you?

453
00:23:10,908 --> 00:23:13,541
Could you take a photo for us?

454
00:23:13,564 --> 00:23:16,198
Sure, no problem!

455
00:23:16,221 --> 00:23:18,555
Can I borrow your camera?

456
00:23:18,578 --> 00:23:20,468
Thanks!

457
00:23:20,491 --> 00:23:23,342
Just press this button.

458
00:23:23,366 --> 00:23:25,766
Got it!

459
00:23:25,789 --> 00:23:28,239
Where should we take it?

460
00:23:28,263 --> 00:23:31,663
I’d love to take it with this rickshaw.

461
00:23:31,686 --> 00:23:35,652
A rickshaw? That’s huge!

462
00:23:35,675 --> 00:23:40,363
Yeah, I’m traveling around Japan with it.

463
00:23:40,387 --> 00:23:43,220
Are you traveling on foot?

464
00:23:43,243 --> 00:23:45,843
Yeah, that's right!

465
00:23:45,866 --> 00:23:47,711
That’s impressive!

466
00:23:47,734 --> 00:23:51,867
I’ll make sure to capture the ocean and the rickshaw.

467
00:23:51,890 --> 00:23:53,357
Thanks!

468
00:23:53,380 --> 00:23:56,051
Okay, I’ll take it!

469
00:23:56,075 --> 00:23:59,361
Say cheese!

470
00:23:59,385 --> 00:24:01,785
I’ll take one more.

471
00:24:01,808 --> 00:24:04,774
Say cheese!

472
00:24:04,797 --> 00:24:06,564
Thanks!

473
00:24:06,587 --> 00:24:08,998
Can I check it?

474
00:24:09,021 --> 00:24:11,498
Here you go.

475
00:24:11,522 --> 00:24:13,055
How does it look?

476
00:24:13,078 --> 00:24:15,765
It’s a fantastic shot!

477
00:24:15,788 --> 00:24:17,393
Thanks!

478
00:24:17,416 --> 00:24:19,493
I’m glad.

479
00:24:19,517 --> 00:24:21,684
It’s such a nice day today.

480
00:24:21,707 --> 00:24:25,873
Yeah, the weather’s perfect.

481
00:24:25,896 --> 00:24:28,330
The scenery is breathtaking.

482
00:24:28,353 --> 00:24:31,323
The ocean and the islands are gorgeous.

483
00:24:31,346 --> 00:24:33,880
Where did you come from?

484
00:24:33,903 --> 00:24:36,748
I walked here all the way from Iwate.

485
00:24:36,771 --> 00:24:40,904
Wow, that’s quite a journey. Where to next?

486
00:24:40,927 --> 00:24:43,661
All the way down south.

487
00:24:43,684 --> 00:24:46,617
That’s a long trip!

488
00:24:46,640 --> 00:24:51,807
But I see new scenery every day.

489
00:24:51,830 --> 00:24:54,505
What do you think of Japan’s scenery?

490
00:24:54,528 --> 00:24:57,094
It’s so beautiful.

491
00:24:57,117 --> 00:24:58,684
I love it.

492
00:24:58,708 --> 00:25:01,441
That makes me happy to hear!

493
00:25:01,464 --> 00:25:04,297
Matsushima is especially beautiful.

494
00:25:04,320 --> 00:25:07,920
Yeah, it's one of my favorite places too.

495
00:25:07,943 --> 00:25:10,800
Thanks for the lovely photos!

496
00:25:10,824 --> 00:25:14,791
You're welcome. Have a safe trip!

497
00:25:14,814 --> 00:25:17,581
Yes, I’ll be careful.

498
00:25:17,604 --> 00:25:19,891
Good luck!

499
00:25:19,915 --> 00:25:21,582
Goodbye.

500
00:25:21,605 --> 00:25:23,338
Goodbye.

501
00:25:23,361 --> 00:25:27,417
I was so moved by the breathtaking views of Matsushima.

502
00:25:27,441 --> 00:25:30,338
I even had someone take a photo of me.

503
00:25:30,361 --> 00:25:35,161
Meeting kind people really brightens my day.

504
00:25:35,184 --> 00:25:39,027
Seeing those beautiful photos really cheered me up.

505
00:25:39,050 --> 00:25:43,327
I’ll head to the next town and keep walking.

506
00:25:43,351 --> 00:25:44,851
Scene 8: How to Use a Japanese Onsen

507
00:25:44,851 --> 00:25:46,251
Hello!

508
00:25:46,274 --> 00:25:49,543
I’m John.

509
00:25:49,567 --> 00:25:53,211
I’ve arrived in Fukushima today.

510
00:25:53,235 --> 00:25:58,121
I’ve walked so much—I’m exhausted.

511
00:25:58,144 --> 00:26:02,111
I’m staying at an onsen ryokan tonight.

512
00:26:02,134 --> 00:26:05,667
I’d love to try a Japanese hot spring.

513
00:26:05,690 --> 00:26:10,309
But I don’t know how to use an onsen.

514
00:26:10,332 --> 00:26:14,866
Let me ask the innkeeper.

515
00:26:14,889 --> 00:26:16,689
Excuse me!

516
00:26:16,712 --> 00:26:19,848
Yes, how can I help you?

517
00:26:19,872 --> 00:26:22,472
I’d like to take a bath in the onsen.

518
00:26:22,495 --> 00:26:25,709
But I’m not sure how to use it.

519
00:26:25,732 --> 00:26:27,932
I see.

520
00:26:27,955 --> 00:26:31,365
Is this your first time at a Japanese onsen?

521
00:26:31,389 --> 00:26:34,840
Yes, it’s my first time.

522
00:26:34,863 --> 00:26:38,076
Could you explain how to use the onsen?

523
00:26:38,099 --> 00:26:39,932
Of course.

524
00:26:39,955 --> 00:26:44,252
First, do I change into a yukata in my room?

525
00:26:44,275 --> 00:26:45,924
Okay.

526
00:26:45,948 --> 00:26:50,148
Change into a yukata first, then go to the onsen.

527
00:26:50,171 --> 00:26:54,704
There’s a place to leave your belongings at the entrance to the onsen.

528
00:26:54,727 --> 00:26:58,409
Do I enter the onsen after undressing?

529
00:26:58,432 --> 00:26:59,921
Okay.

530
00:26:59,945 --> 00:27:04,217
Please remove all your clothes, including your underwear, before entering.

531
00:27:04,240 --> 00:27:07,050
Can I wear a swimsuit?

532
00:27:07,074 --> 00:27:10,674
No, you must not wear a swimsuit.

533
00:27:10,697 --> 00:27:12,716
Of course.

534
00:27:12,740 --> 00:27:15,906
Can I bring a towel inside?

535
00:27:15,929 --> 00:27:20,529
Yes, you may bring a small towel with you.

536
00:27:20,552 --> 00:27:25,025
Do I enter the hot water right after going in?

537
00:27:25,049 --> 00:27:30,300
No, you should wash your body before entering the hot water.

538
00:27:30,323 --> 00:27:34,794
Wash your body first, then soak in the hot water.

539
00:27:34,817 --> 00:27:37,509
Yeah, that's right!

540
00:27:37,533 --> 00:27:41,143
Please wash your hair before entering the onsen.

541
00:27:41,166 --> 00:27:43,206
Of course.

542
00:27:43,230 --> 00:27:46,897
Can I put the towel in the hot water?

543
00:27:46,919 --> 00:27:51,690
No, do not put the towel in the hot water.

544
00:27:51,714 --> 00:27:55,914
Can I place the towel on my head?

545
00:27:55,937 --> 00:27:59,508
Yes, that’s fine.

546
00:27:59,532 --> 00:28:02,818
Can I wash my body in the hot water?

547
00:28:02,841 --> 00:28:07,774
No, do not wash your body in the hot water.

548
00:28:07,797 --> 00:28:10,615
Yes, I’ll be careful.

549
00:28:10,639 --> 00:28:13,081
Is the hot spring water hot?

550
00:28:13,105 --> 00:28:16,717
It might be a little hot.

551
00:28:16,740 --> 00:28:18,584
Of course.

552
00:28:18,608 --> 00:28:22,341
After soaking in the onsen, I’ll rest in my room.

553
00:28:22,364 --> 00:28:26,233
Yes, please relax and take it easy.

554
00:28:26,256 --> 00:28:28,323
Thanks!

555
00:28:28,346 --> 00:28:30,123
I’m off!

556
00:28:30,146 --> 00:28:33,546
Have a good one!

557
00:28:33,569 --> 00:28:36,902
The onsen was wonderfully warm.

558
00:28:36,925 --> 00:28:39,799
All my fatigue is gone.

559
00:28:39,823 --> 00:28:44,492
I felt at ease because I learned how to enter properly before getting in.

560
00:28:44,516 --> 00:28:48,165
The hot springs in Fukushima are the best!

561
00:28:48,188 --> 00:28:52,823
And that marks the end of my journey through Hokkaido and Tohoku.

562
00:28:52,846 --> 00:28:55,980
I’ve seen so many famous spots.

563
00:28:56,003 --> 00:28:59,407
I met so many kind people along the way.

564
00:28:59,430 --> 00:29:03,863
Next up, my journey through Kanto and Chubu begins.

565
00:29:03,886 --> 00:29:07,653
I’ll keep enjoying my travels in Japan even more.

566
00:29:07,676 --> 00:29:10,520
See you in the next video!

567
00:29:20,179 --> 00:29:21,679
Scene 1: Journey Across Japan – From North to South

568
